WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Ductwork is where most systems lose efficiency. Learn to read it and you'll find
problems other techs miss.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Side-by-side comparison of Type I, II, and III requirements. Recovery levels,
leak repair triggers, equipment types, and system examples for each type.
Understanding the differences between types is critical because the Universal

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Here's why this matters on the job: The Universal exam tests your ability to
distinguish between types. Confusion between Type II and III recovery levels is
the most common exam failure.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Watch out for these: Type II under 200 lbs = 0 psig, over 200 lbs = 10 in Hg
vacuum. And — Type III under 200 lbs = 0 psig, over 200 lbs = 25 mm Hg absolute

